course: dictionary
lesson: 1380
title: One word, three meanings: capital
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word capital has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one is meant. Ask: what would fit here? «The capital of Australia is Canberra» is about a city, because a city fits and a letter or money would not make sense.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Ireland is the green island with Dublin as its capital.» If you swap in "big letter", it makes no sense, so capital means the city where the government is.
explain: Capital letters are different. They are the big letters, like A, B and C, and in English we use them at the start of a sentence, for names of people and places, for «I», and for days and months. Clues like "name" or "sentence" point you to the letter meaning.
explain: In business, capital means money used to start or run a shop or company. If a sentence talks about money, a shop or a business, look for this meaning. Always check the clues around the word first.
fact: A capital is the city where a country's or state's government is.
fact: «The capital of the United States is Washington, D.C.»
fact: A capital letter is a big letter, like A, B or C.
fact: Capital is money used to start or run a business.
fact: Capital punishment is the punishment of death, in law.
exercise: «The capital of Australia is Canberra, built as a compromise between Sydney and Melbourne.» In this sentence, what does capital mean? | A big letter | Money for a business | *The city where the government is | Punishment of death
exercise: The walk to the lake ended in Dublin. Which word is a place name, so it needs a capital letter? | *Dublin | walk | ended | lake
exercise: Mum says, «The shop needs more capital before it can open.» What does capital mean here? | *Money to start or run a business | Punishment of death | A big letter | The city where the government is
test: «Lebanon's capital is Beirut.» What is a capital in this sentence? | *A city where the government is | Punishment of death | Money for a shop | A big letter
test: Which word should start with a capital letter because it is a place name? | bridge | river | mountain | *London
exam: Ella reads, «The shop needs more capital to open.» What does capital mean? | The city where the government is | A big letter | Punishment of death | *Money to start a business
